6 contratos menores de servicios y suministros de más de 14.000 y hasta 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 7,6 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 4,7, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 2,9 a 7,7. En diciembre se adjudicó el 3 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 6 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 26 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.980 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos ilícitos. Puede deberse a precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No implica que se haya partido ningún contrato ni que haya existido negligencia.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en años distintos. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o ajustes de gasto.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 36 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 7.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.9 to 7.7. December accounts for 3% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 7. Contract [1], for 14,980 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts are just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices may be set by market conditions or budget constraints, and small differences don't always indicate improper actions.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the dates. Also review awardee A's contracts to see if multiple contracts cover the same need. Look for patterns in the timing of awards to understand if there's a recurring issue.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["PgqpmlWF0XkeIBJRHQiPkQ%3D%3D","kISUpXumyUfkY6rls5tG9A%3D%3D","vtZ8T4mzxR%2Bzz8fXU2i3eQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}